          "quote": "Net-(U10-RXD) : U10.2(RXD,output) U9.2(RXCAN,input)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(U10-TXD) : U10.3(TXD,input) U9.1(TXCAN,output)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver (`U11`/companion)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN0 controller TX and RX lines are effectively shorted together and driven by the transceiver RXD output. CAN0 communication would fail, and the TX/RX LED indicators would not reflect correct activity.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist contains a clear connectivity anomaly: U11.2 appears on both TXLED and RXLED, bridging the CAN0 TX and RX paths, while U11.3 is missing from the expected TXLED net."
